<title>UK: UK traders bid for free-market wheat, no details.</title>
<headline>UK traders bid for free-market wheat, no details.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK grain traders placed bids for free market wheat export refunds, the UK Intervention Board for Agricultural Produce said on Thursday.</p>
<p>However, the board was unable to give any details.</p>
<p>&quot;There have been less than three bids so we are unable to give any details,&quot; the Board said.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
</text>
